Protected member access– Employee and Developer

📌 Description

This C++ program demonstrates Single Inheritance using two classes: "Employee" and "Developer".

The "Developer" class inherits the "name" property from the "Employee" class and adds its own "language" property.

---

📚 Classes Used

1. "Employee" Class

The "Employee" class is the base class.

It contains:

- "name" – Stores the employee's name.
- Constructor – Initializes the employee's name.
- "protected" access specifier – Allows the derived "Developer" class to access "name".

2. "Developer" Class

The "Developer" class is the derived class of "Employee".

It contains:

- "language" – Stores the programming language.
- Constructor – Initializes the employee's name and programming language.
- "display()" – Displays the developer's details.

---

⚙️ Main Function

In the "main()" function:

1. A "Developer" object is created.
2. The name "Neha" and programming language "C++" are passed to the constructor.
3. The "display()" function is called to display the details.

---

🖥️ Output

Developer: Neha
Language: C++

---

🧠 OOP Concept Used

Single Inheritance

Employee
    ↓
Developer

Here:

- "Employee" → Base Class
- "Developer" → Derived Class
- Inheritance Type → Single Inheritance

